.TH ORO-CLIPBOARD 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:clipboard \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:clipboard'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Cross\-environment helpers for interacting with the system clipboard. In browser contexts this delegates to the standard `navigator.clipboard` API, falling back to a temporary textarea when direct access is not available. In non\-browser runtimes the helpers reject with a descriptive error so callers can present a friendly message.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBwriteText(text)\fR
Write a string to the system clipboard.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItext\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBreadText()\fR
Read the current text contents from the system clipboard.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<string>\fR
.TP
\fBcanWriteText()\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR True when clipboard write operations are supported.
.TP
\fBcanReadText()\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR True when clipboard read operations are supported.
